; -*- mode: lisp -*-
; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
; AUTHORED. See weave4.task for the shared design: the spool fixture, the seat
; geometry and the 8.25 mm it is pinned to, the worst_of grouping and the zero
; idle floor. See weave5.task for what a LEVEL is; this is the top of that
; ladder.
;
; L3. Six stations at weave_stagger's full 25 mm depth: 232.2 degrees of
; accumulated turning, which is two thirds of a turn and the most of any
; arrangement this suite ships.
;
;   weave3   3 stations   scatter     12.6 deg   L1
;   weave4   4 stations   0    mm     36.5 deg   L1
;   weave5   5 stations  12.5  mm    119.9 deg   L2
;   weave6   6 stations  25    mm    232.2 deg   L3   <- this one
;
; PAST HALF A TURN THE ROUTE STOPS BEING DRIVEABLE FROM ONE END, and that is
; what the top band is for rather than "more of the same". Tension through a
; route falls as exp(-mu * Theta), so a pull at the free end arrives at the far
; station with 30% of its strength here against weave4's 83%. There is no drag
; that reaches the whole route. Every station has to be given its own slack,
; from a hand that is already there, and the support arm's feed stops being a
; correction and becomes the mechanism.
;
; NOTHING IN THIS SUITE IS L4, and that is a measurement rather than an
; omission. Reaching a full turn on a 155 mm pitch needs a ninth station or a
; stagger deeper than the working arm's envelope allows -- the band any board
; may stand in is 80 mm wide -- and adding either to make a table look complete
; would be adding a task to fit a label. See difficulty.py, where the ladder
; moved when the pitch did.
;
; THE ROD IS 1.15 m AT 96 CAPSULES. Five crossings of 2 * (25 + 8.25) mm need a
; long rod, and a long rod at weave4's constant 42 would be a COARSE one --
; 27.4 mm per capsule against 11.9. A 90 degree station turn around the 8.25 mm
; seated radius spans about 13 mm of arc, so at 42 the entire turn would fall
; inside a single capsule and the rod would corner rather than bend. 96 holds
; the family's pitch. See weave_segments in assets/cable.py.
;
; WHICH IS WHY THE SHARE IS 0.039 AND NOT 0.047. Both ask for about the same
; LENGTH of rod in the box -- 0.039 of 96 capsules is 3.7 bodies, or 45 mm,
; against weave4's 0.047 of 42 at 19 mm pitch, which is 2 bodies and 38 mm. The
; share moved because the rod did; what it asks for did not.
;
; ONE THING THIS BOARD DOES NOT HAVE. Its near row stands at x = 0.495, the
; nearest in the family, so its near-side seat boxes reach back to 0.450 -- and
; the rod's whole spawn envelope reaches 0.480, which is 29.9 mm inside one of
; them. That is the widest breach of any layout here. Against the BOW alone,
; which is the term the 0.42 spawn line was sized against, it still clears by
; 10 mm. WEAVE_CABLE_WAVE in assets/cable.py has the per-layout table and says
; what the envelope is and is not: no rollout has measured an idle score at
; these constants.
; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

(define (problem WEAVE_THE_CABLE_THROUGH_SIX_STAGGERED_PEGS)

  (:suite cable_route)

  (:language weave the cable between the six staggered pegs, alternating sides)

  (:staging
    (:cameras cable_weave6@v1)
    ; The longest in the family by half again: five crossings at
    ; weave_stagger's 66.5 mm of x-travel each, on a rod a quarter longer than
    ; its own, and a support feed at every one of them.
    (:max-steps 12000)
    ; The rod's own shape and placement, drawn per episode; the board does not
    ; move. See weave4.
    (:episodes (:count 8) (:seed 0) (:sampler staging:CABLE_BOW))
  )

  (:objects
    cable - weave6_cable
  )

  (:fixtures
    peg0 - weave6_peg0
    peg1 - weave6_peg1
    peg2 - weave6_peg2
    peg3 - weave6_peg3
    peg4 - weave6_peg4
    peg5 - weave6_peg5
  )

  ; -------------------------------------------------------------------------
  ; Six stations, two rows, alternating sides -1, +1, -1, +1, -1, +1 -- and the
  ; seats are still weave4's box, stated in each station's own frame. Two
  ; different world x, one definition of "seated on the near side".
  (:regions
    (seat0 (:target peg0) (:ranges ((-0.045 -0.035 -0.003 0.035))))
    (seat1 (:target peg1) (:ranges (( 0.003 -0.035  0.045 0.035))))
    (seat2 (:target peg2) (:ranges ((-0.045 -0.035 -0.003 0.035))))
    (seat3 (:target peg3) (:ranges (( 0.003 -0.035  0.045 0.035))))
    (seat4 (:target peg4) (:ranges ((-0.045 -0.035 -0.003 0.035))))
    (seat5 (:target peg5) (:ranges (( 0.003 -0.035  0.045 0.035))))
  )

  ; No init constraint: both arms at home, touching nothing. See weave4.
  (:init)

  (:goal
    (worst_of
      (And
        (>= (containment cable seat0) 0.039)
        (>= (containment cable seat1) 0.039)
        (>= (containment cable seat2) 0.039)
        (>= (containment cable seat3) 0.039)
        (>= (containment cable seat4) 0.039)
        (>= (containment cable seat5) 0.039)
      )
      (And
        (> (tcp-distance cable) 0.05)
        (<= (speed cable) 0.05)
      )
    )
  )

  (:observe
    (once (<= (tcp-distance cable) 0.05))
    (straightness cable)
  )

  ; The same motion three ways: a routine, the oracle graph, and the vision
  ; graph that runs the same crossing loop off the `cable` camera. See weave4.
  (:artifacts
    (:routine "routine:RoutineWeave")
    (:graph gt "graphs/weave")
    (:graph vision "graphs/weave_vision")
  )

  (:provenance
    (:tier authored)
    (:source "this stack -- the L3 rung of the cable_route difficulty ladder")
    (:note "Six F1 spools on weave4's 155 mm y-pitch, offset +/-25 mm in x and phased against
            the required sides -- weave_stagger's geometry carried to six stations.
            Accumulated turning of the scored route is 232.2 deg at a mean crossing obliquity
            of 23.2 deg, the most of any arrangement here; see tasks/cable_route/difficulty.py.
            The rod is 1.15 m at 96 capsules, discretised at the family's 11.9 mm pitch rather
            than at weave4's constant count, which is why the share is 0.039 rather than 0.047
            -- both are about 45 mm of rod in a 70 mm box. The seated route is 923 mm with its
            tails, clearing WEAVE_MIN_SLACK by 207 mm. Reach-checked against rigs/weave_reach.py:
            the right arm's band is y in [-0.36, +0.10] over the x this layout spans, and the
            stations run y = -0.448 to +0.328, so both ends of this board sit past it -- the
            widest layout in the suite and the one whose outer stations the routine reaches by
            chaining rather than from home. The support anchor at WEAVE_ANCHOR_Y = 0.17 sits
            BETWEEN the outermost two stations here rather than clear of them, which is the
            defect weave_anchor_y fixes for the terminated runs and deliberately does not fix
            for the plain weaves. No scripted routine of its own.")
  )
)
